{"shortDescription":"India's first-ever tokenised corporate bond sale concluded successfully as state-run REC NSE:RECLTD accepted bids worth 5 billion rupees ($52.94 million) for bonds maturing in one year and eight months, three merchant bankers said on Monday.REC accepted bids for the bond issue at an annual coupon o…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["India's first-ever tokenised corporate bond sale concluded successfully as state-run REC ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NSE:RECLTD","text":"NSE:RECLTD"}}," accepted bids worth 5 billion rupees ($52.94 million) for bonds maturing in one year and eight months, three merchant bankers said on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["REC accepted bids for the bond issue at an annual coupon of 7.30%, the bankers said, adding that the notes would be settled before the end of Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Tokenised bonds are securities whose ownership, issuance, trading and settlement are recorded digitally on a blockchain or distributed ledger. The Reserve Bank of India's digital currency will be used to buy the bonds."]},{"type":"p","children":["This is India's first debt issue to use blockchain technology to enable instant settlements of bond transactions, placing the country alongside markets such as Europe and Hong Kong in using the technology for issuance and settlement."]},{"type":"p","children":["Only investors with active security and CBDC wallets were allowed to place bids for the issue."]},{"type":"p","children":["REC did not respond to a Reuters email seeking comment."]},{"type":"p","children":["Here is the list of deals reported so far on September 7:"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Issuer"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Tenure"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Coupon (in %)